From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Windows 11's popup menus as the prototype draws them

The approved Windows 11 prototype (prototypes/windows11-shell, css/ui.css .menu) draws every menu as a rounded acrylic
flyout: rows 32 px tall 4 px inside the list, an icon column and labels 11 and 39 px into a row, shortcuts in caption
text and a 12 px chevron ending 11 px from its right edge, 1 px separators with 2 px around them, a 28 px plate with
4 px corners under the hovered row and a focus ring round it once the keyboard drives the menu. Wine drew the classic
square menu: a raised edge, the highlight colour across the row, Wine's own check and arrow bitmaps. The shell
scorecard's menu states matched none of the prototype's pixels (evidence/shell-scorecard-2026-10-16-01.json).

Every popup (#32768: context menus, menu bar drop-downs, the window menu, in every program) now
- asks the compositor for the prototype's flyout (DWMWA_SYSTEMBACKDROP_TYPE PS5_DWMSBT_FLYOUT, round corners, a sheet
  of glass, dark when COLOR_MENU is): the acrylic, the 8 px corners, the stroke and --shadow-28;
- lays out its items as src/pw_menu_style.h measures the prototype (calc_popup_menu_size): a check column when an
  item can be checked, an icon column when one has a picture, at least 200 px wide, at most 456 (labels then end in an
  ellipsis); a popup's first items with a picture and no text are Windows 11's command row, 40 x 40 cells that
  centre their pictures;
- paints itself through one premultiplied buffer over that glass (draw_popup_menu): the plates, ring, separators,
  check, radio dot and chevron are the prototype's own pixels (pw_menu_sprites.h, tools/build-menu-sprites.py);
  labels (14 px) and shortcuts (12 px) are Chromium's own glyphs (pw_menu_glyphs.h, src/pw_text_glyphs.h: the
  prototype's .menu-label and .menu-shortcut at Skia's four pen phases) at their linear advances, the menu's width the
  widest row rounded once and right-aligned shortcuts ending at that row's fractional edge, as Chromium lays them out;
  text the glyphs lack (and the default item's semibold) is each glyph's 256-level coverage composed with Skia's mask
  gamma in the TextFillColor tokens; 32-bit pictures are composed with their alpha, others
  copied opaque; owner-drawn items and HBMMENU_CALLBACK pictures are drawn by their owner on the menu's opaque colour;
- repaints a row through that buffer when its selection changes (select_item), never piecemeal over the glass;
- opens a submenu over its parent's 4 px edge with its first row level with the parent's row, on the left when the
  right has no room (show_sub_popup);
- shows the keyboard ring from the first navigation key and access-key underlines from then on, and hides the ring
  when the pointer moves (track_menu).
Without the compositor (the server refuses the attributes off the console) the same menu is drawn opaque.
---
